 def assert (p : Bool) (s : String) : PreSailM RegisterType c ue Unit :=
   if p then pure () else throw (.Assertion s)
 
+/-- Lean's `do` notation reserves `assert` as a verification-condition element. Generated Sail
+code calls `assert cond msg` as a plain monadic action, so redirect that element to the
+`Sail.assert` specialization the Sail backend emits for the model. The target identifier is
+built with `mkIdent` so it is resolved at the call site, where that specialization is in scope. -/
+macro_rules
+  | `(doElem| assert $cond:term $msg:term) =>
+    `(doElem| $(Lean.mkIdent `Sail.assert):ident $cond $msg)
+
